# Optional browser runtime

<!-- Generated by scripts/generate-v1-guides.ts from executed canonical source. Do not edit this output by hand. -->

V2-02 adds the first optional browser-only entrypoint. It is a loading and
private transport boundary, not enhanced navigation yet. Native links and forms
remain the complete behavior, and importing the browser facade alone performs
no startup work.

The application build owns a generated entry that imports only the public
browser facade and starts it explicitly:

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/browser-runtime/browser-entry.ts","language":"ts"} -->

The current packed-package gate renders that entry through the real renderer,
links it to browser files from the same installed tarball, and runs it in all
three supported browser engines. The normalized successful observation is:

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/browser-runtime/expected/success.json","language":"json"} -->

Startup outside a browser document is a stable refusal and does not expose a
second runtime mode:

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/browser-runtime/expected/refusal.json","language":"json"} -->

The flow record makes the current ownership and deliberately skipped work
explicit:

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/browser-runtime/expected/flow.json","language":"json"} -->

Wrong or missing nonce, a missing module, disabled JavaScript, and operational
rollback all leave the native page usable. Rollback stops module emission and
restores the renderer's `script-src 'none'` policy:

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/browser-runtime/expected/recovery.json","language":"json"} -->

Run `pnpm check:v2-browser-runtime` for the clean packed consumer and 18
three-engine cases. Run `pnpm check:v2-patch-protocol` for exact envelope,
malformed input, raw byte, structural depth/count, duration, cancellation,
cross-generation isolation, and redaction evidence. The update protocol remains
private, and no analyzer/editor schema is added.

## Server-owned outcome projection

V2-03 can turn the complete native response already produced by routing,
resources, actions, sessions, and rendering into the private update envelope.
It does not run any of that application work a second time. This remains server
infrastructure: no link or form is intercepted and no browser document is
changed yet.

The canonical scenario is ordinary application code using only public package
entrypoints:

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/server-update/application.ts","language":"ts"} -->

The packed gate compares the native response with the projected document and
records the application invocation counts:

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/server-update/expected/success.json","language":"json"} -->

An expected action failure retains its accessible server-rendered messages and
stable action code:

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/server-update/expected/expected-failure.json","language":"json"} -->

Authorization or ownership refusal publishes no envelope. There is no safe
automatic correction for an ownership refusal: the native response remains the
authority, and a mutation must never be repeated to manufacture projection
ownership.

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/server-update/expected/refusal-human.txt","language":"text"} -->

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/server-update/expected/refusal.json","language":"json"} -->

The redacted flow record preserves causes and ownership without markup,
credentials, proofs, session values, or submitted fields:

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/server-update/expected/flow.json","language":"json"} -->

Duplicate results and cross-owner responses refuse. A fresh navigation contains
no stale action failure or result identity, while the native response remains
usable when projection rolls back:

<!-- fadeno:include {"path":"examples/v1-app/scenarios/server-update/expected/recovery.json","language":"json"} -->

Run `pnpm check:v2-server-update` for direct boundary tests plus the clean
packed application. The projector, its record, and the envelope remain private;
V2-04 owns the first enhanced link navigation.

